# /github_kit fast-path trigger

If the human's message starts with `/github_kit` followed by a task description, treat that
invocation itself as the human's approval for the described task — do not also wait for the
separate `approve` phrase. The approval is scoped strictly to the task text
supplied in that message; if the work turns out to need more than that description covers, stop
and use the normal approval gate (`approve`) for the additional scope.

Everything else about the workflow is unchanged from `agent-workflow.mdc`: still produce a visible
plan, still create the GitHub issue and track it on the Project, still branch with the configured
agent prefix, still validate with the commands in `docs/ai/PROJECT_CONFIG.md`, still open the PR as
**draft** using `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`, still never merge or push to the base/production
branch, still write a handoff file before stopping mid-task.

This trigger is additive — `approve` remains the default gate for any task not
invoked via `/github_kit`. See `docs/ai/AGENT_WORKFLOW.md` → "Fast-path trigger: /github_kit" for
the full spec.
